  "reason": "Evidence: RNA (PCA n2000, single profile) achieves 0.485 accuracy while Image (ResNet50, single profile) is weak at 0.208, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. The single biggest untested lever for the dominant modality is the RNA encoder choice. Question: Does a learned generative encoder (scVI, n=200 latent) outperform the linear PCA (n=2000) representation? Config_004 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) isolates exactly this variable against the config_001 baseline while holding profile setting and aggregation constant. Why this is the best next experiment: With only 2 of 10 experiments done, reducing uncertainty about the RNA encoder is the highest-value information gain. If scVI substantially improves over PCA, it redirects the entire search toward learned encoders for both unimodal and multimodal configs; if it does not, PCA remains the backbone and we can focus budget on profile/aggregation/fusion choices. This single comparison maximally narrows the design space for the remaining 7 experiments."
}

